  "rationale": "The fleet facts are clear: iterative dominates (14/17 front designs, best area 345), unrolled_k is a distant second (3/17, best 446), pipelined families are far off (843-1493) and contribute nothing to the front. For this low-area spec with throughput >= 1 MSPS, iterative is the primary candidate. The key tradeoff is accuracy_bits vs luts_plus_ffs: I need to find the minimum-area design that meets max_abs_err <= 2^-10 (accuracy_bits >= 10) while maintaining throughput >= 1 MSPS. data_width 12-16 with n_iter 10-14 covers the accuracy boundary. angle_guard negative saves LUTs. I'll spend 70% on iterative (the front owner) and 30% on unrolled_k (to confirm no better tradeoff exists). Both families share the same accuracy parameters, so the search regions are aligned. The 100-eval budget is split 70/30."
